Z||000000||x-thumpr-x||12-16-2001||10:43 PM||||I finally got my black 85GT drivable today. Took it on the side road that leads into the storage unit (temp home) and she runs sweet. Just a WEEEEEEEEE bit more UMPHHHH then my 84 coupe.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Still have a couple of touch-ups to do (tighten throttle cable, tighten exhuast bolts for Y-pipe/cat joint, brake job & e-brake line) But next summer (after paint job!) it should be fun driving her while my G/F gets to drive the coupe.  <P>The owner was gonna scrap the car but sold it to me instead for $50. I put little over $300 (can$)into the car and she runs fine. <P><BR>I have a white 85GT also. Was gonna be the g/f's car but previous owner severly aboused it. Cradle really deformed and alot of hidden rust so, I'm gonna strip off the car what I need for the black GT then sell parts of the car to whoever needs them. Like to stick the the GTA and surrounding area's though. Never mailed a part in my life!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> <P>Hey Lothar, now I can keep up with you, bob, & tim (as long as any P/A isn't used!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pasfc.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LArear.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> Where there's a Willie, there's a way!<P>red 84 coupe (running)<BR>white 85GT   (not)<BR>black 85GT   ( she running now! almost done)<P>Willie.. :-)||||reg||10
